-- title:
--   Blow-up charts: primes over the supersingular point are maximal
-- statement:
--   **Arithmetic and geometric data.** Let $q$ be a prime with $q\ge 5$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ and $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; the hypothesis `hι` asks that some ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ send $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq L(\!(t)\!)$ (Laurent series over $L$) which, by `hK`, is [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of the function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), i.e. the subfield of $L(\!(t)\!)$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_H$, $N_0=(q\ell)^2M'$, $H=\ker\big((\mathbb Z/N_0)^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times\big)$. Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation ring which is an $L$-subalgebra with $L$ as fraction field, with algebraically closed residue field, with $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ and with $\xi$ in the image of $A$, and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j\in K$, $j\ne0$, be the element whose Laurent expansion is the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular $j$-function. Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak m_A$, and let $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   Write $C=$ `chartAlgFin A K j`, the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, and $\mathfrak X=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the two chart algebras along the middle chart, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and with `ιFin : Spec C ⟶ 𝔛`.
--
--   **The supersingular centre.** Let $y\subset C$ be a maximal ideal containing the image of $\varpi$, and let `hss` require that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), that is: every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   **The Drinfeld chart hypothesis `hArig`.** This hypothesis postulates, for every point $z$ of $\mathfrak X$, every element $\varpi_z$ of the stalk $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ equal to the germ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under `toBase`, lying in the maximal ideal of that stalk, and every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec}C$ with `ιFin` $(y')=z$ whose ideal satisfies the same supersingularity condition as $y$ above, the existence of: a complete discrete valuation ring $W$ with a ring map $\sigma:A\to W$ such that $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$; power series $f,u,v\in W[\![X_0,X_1]\!]$ with $u,v$ units and $f\equiv$ [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18) $=X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$; and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ onto $S=W[\![X_0,X_1]\!]/\big(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v-fu\big)$. Writing `toC` for the completion map, `mkS` for the quotient map onto $S$, and `germY` for the germ map $C\to\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ through `ιFin`, seven conditions are required: (1) $e$ carries the image of $a\in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$; (2) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau\in\operatorname{Aut}_L(K)$ which is a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ in the sense of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) (for every ratio of modular forms of weight $k$ and level $\Gamma_H(N_0)$ with integral $q$-expansions representing an element $x$ of $K$, and every embedding $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$, the series $\iota(\tau x)$ is the corresponding ratio of $q$-expansions of the forms pulled back along `conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹`), $\tau$ maps $C$ into $C$; (3) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\cap\Gamma(\ell)$ and such a $\tau$ preserving $C$, the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$ is the identity modulo $y'$; (4) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and such a $\tau$ preserving $C$ and trivial modulo $y'$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c\in W$ and a matrix $M\in M_2(W)$ such that $\theta$ intertwines $e\circ{}$`toC`$\circ{}$`germY` with the same map composed with $\tau$, $\theta$ fixes the classes of constants, $\theta(X_j)\equiv\sum_i C(M_{ij})X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$, $c^{q+1}\equiv1$ and $M_{ij}\equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_W$, $c\equiv1$ if $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, and $c\not\equiv1$ if $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\ne\mathrm{id}$; (5) separation of branches: for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S$ each omitting at least one of the classes of $X_0,X_1$, each containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$, and each containing an element of the form $C(a_i)X_0+C(b_i)X_1$ plus a term in $(X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1,P_2$ along $e\circ{}$`toC` differ; (6) for a prime $P$ of $S$ as in (5) containing such an element with $(a,b)=(1,0)$, and for $a\in C$, the germ of $a$ lies in the contraction of $P$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$; (7) [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0\in A$ with the difference of that element and $a_0$ in $y'$, an integer $e_0\ge1$ and $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ whose degree-$e_0$ form $\sum_{i\le e_0}\operatorname{coeff}_{(i,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit for all $a,b\in W$ with $a$ or $b$ a unit and $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_W$, such that $e$ maps the germ of that difference to the class of $h$.
--
--   **A fixed witness.** Data $z,\varpi_z$ (with `hϖz`, `hz` as above), $y'$ with `hy'` and the supersingularity condition `hss'`, and `hy'y` identifying $y'$ with $y$, are fixed; together with a witness $W_1,\sigma_1,f_1,u_1,v_1,e_1$ as in `hArig` (with $u_1,v_1$ units, $\mathfrak m_{W_1}=(\sigma_1\varpi)$, $f_1\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ mod $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$), and the hypothesis `hW₁`, which asserts for this witness exactly the seven conditions (1)–(7) listed above.
--
--   **The centre $J$, the blow-up algebra $B$ and the valuation ring $W$.** The hypothesis `hJ` defines $J\subseteq C$ to be the infimum of the ideals $\tau^{-1}\big((e_1\circ{}$`toC`$\circ{}$`germY`$)^{-1}\big(\text{span}\{\mathrm{mkS}\,C(\sigma_1\varpi_t),\ \mathrm{mkS}\,X_0,\ \mathrm{mkS}\,X_1\}\big)\big)$ taken over all $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and all level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ which preserve $C$. The hypothesis `hB` sets $B=C\big[\{x\in K:\ x\varpi_t\in J\}\big]$, viewed as an $A$-subalgebra of $K$. Finally $W$ is a valuation subring of $K$ with $B\subseteq W$ (`hBW`), subject to four groups of hypotheses: `hR1` states that $C\subseteq B$ and that every element of $K$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$, $h\ne0$; `hR2` states that $A\to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation and that $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses) states that an element of $L$ lies in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$, that $\mathfrak m_W$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that an element of $C$ lies in $y$ exactly when it lies in $W$ with class in $\mathfrak m_W$, and that $f\in K$ lies in $W$ exactly when $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $h\notin\mathfrak m_W$; and `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here) states that for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho$ from $B$ onto [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with kernel the elements of $\mathfrak m_W$, compatible with $A\to$ residue field, and equivariant for level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W$, through an element $c$ of $\mathbb F_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,c)$ in the subgroup [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) acting by [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325), with $c\ne1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\ne\mathrm{id}$; that such $\tau$ preserve $B$; that every prime $Q$ of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is reached from the centre of $W$ by some $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and corresponding $\tau$; that an element of $B$ all of whose translates by such pairs lie in $\mathfrak m_W$ is divisible by $\varpi$; and that a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$, $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, preserving $y$ in $C$ also preserves $W$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under these hypotheses, for every $a\in C$ with $a\in J$ and $a\ne0$ in $K$, set
--   $$B_a=C\big[\{x\in K:\ \exists\, i\in J,\ x\,a=i\}\big]\subseteq K,$$
--   an $A$-subalgebra of $K$. Then every prime ideal $Q$ of $B_a$ with the two properties
--
--   (i) for every $c\in C$ with $c\in y$ whose image in $K$ lies in $B_a$, that image belongs to $Q$, and
--
--   (ii) whenever $\varpi_t\cdot a^{-1}$ (the image of $\varpi_t$ in $K$ divided by $a$) lies in $B_a$, that element belongs to $Q$,
--
--   is a maximal ideal of $B_a$.
--
--   This is the case of the trichotomy for primes of the blow-up of the supersingular chart in which the prime lies over the supersingular centre and contains the ratio $\varpi_t/a$: on each affine chart $C[J/a]$ of the blow-up of $C$ along the weighted centre $J$, such a prime is maximal, which expresses that the corresponding locus on the exceptional fibre is finite. It is used in the proof of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.blowupChart_primes_over_supersingular_exceptional_generic_or_end_on_unique_component_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.blowupChart_primes_over_supersingular_exceptional_generic_or_end_on_unique_component_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked), the statement that primes over a supersingular point of the blow-up chart are either generic, or on a unique component, or of this exceptional type.
